{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Let terror and dread fall upon them by the greatness of Your arm.</b> May it be Your will that terror and dread fall upon them, so that they flee before us in fear of Your arm — as in: אָנוּסָה מִפְּנֵי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי ה׳ נִלְחָם (Exodus 14:25)." "<b>They are still as stone until Your people pass by, O YHWH.</b> And likewise may it be Your will that they not rise against us when we march up to do battle with them, until after we cross the rivers — the Arnon and the Jordan — for indeed at a river-crossing every war is difficult, and we would need a great miracle for which perhaps we would not be worthy."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:41.305464472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}